{
 "_about": "How names and recurring terms are written in this language. Every translation follows this file, so a name is always spelled the same way. Names are written by sound, never translated (the author's rule). The spellings here are first versions based on the written names: the author's own pronunciation is recorded in Legacy/Behind The Scenes/World Lore/Word Pronunciation/Unique Words Pronounciation.wav, so correct any spelling here and later translations will follow it. Add new names the first time they are translated.",
 "rule": "Story names in Hangul, by sound. This covers coined world terms too: creatures, plants, items, nari gels, spells, factions, guilds, places, ranks and coins (Wood People = 우드 피플, Sapphire = 사파이어, Bleed Out = 블리드 아웃). Parts of names are separated by spaces, as Korean writes foreign names (해리 산비, 아루키아 롱 브리지). Japanese-origin names follow the usual Korean spelling of Japanese (히로미, 다케오, 요스케). Plain words are translated (Nari Stones = 나리석, Black Honey = 검은 꿀). The currency balls is 볼 (사파이어 볼); the unit timehunk stays in Latin letters. Real people (Deovandski, Mitsukiven, Feiourm), the title and pets named in the afterwords (Peeta, Fluffy, Maddog) stay in Latin letters.",
 "keep_as_is": [
  "A Husband Out of This World",
  "#HusbandOutWorld",
  "Deovandski",
  "Deovandski Skibinski Junior",
  "Mitsukiven",
  "Feiourm",
